SONORA – iOS Music Player

Complete Project Requirements & Development Handover

1. Project Overview

I want to build my own premium music player application for iPhone.

App Name: SONORA

Primary Objective:
Build a high-quality music player without advertisements, mandatory subscriptions or unnecessary restrictions.

I want to own and control my music library, store my music in cloud storage and play it on my iPhone without consuming too much device storage.

This is initially a personal-use application. I may consider publishing it on the Apple App Store in the future.

I have a Mac mini and an iPhone.

⸻

2. Platform and Technology

* Platform: iOS
* Development language: Swift
* UI framework: SwiftUI
* Audio playback: AVFoundation
* Advanced audio processing: AVAudioEngine
* Local database: SwiftData or SQLite
* Development environment: Xcode
* Native iOS application preferred over Flutter or React Native.

The application should be designed to support future expansion.

⸻

3. Application Design

I want a premium, modern and minimal interface.

Preferred design direction:

* Dark-themed interface.
* Premium music-player appearance.
* Smooth animations.
* Album artwork prominently displayed.
* Simple navigation.
* Fast loading.
* Easy access to music controls.

Suggested sections:

1. Home
2. Search
3. My Library
4. Cloud Storage
5. Upload Music
6. Downloads
7. Equalizer
8. Settings

The navigation structure can be improved during development.

⸻

4. Music Sources

The application should support multiple music sources.

A. iPhone Local Storage

* Import music from the iPhone Files app.
* Support files downloaded through Safari.
* Import multiple songs.
* Read available audio metadata.
* Automatically organize music by artist and album.
* Display album artwork when available.

B. Cloud Storage

Support these cloud providers:

* Google Drive
* MEGA
* Microsoft OneDrive
* Dropbox

Users should be able to connect their own accounts through secure authentication.

Important requirements:

* Browse cloud folders.
* Search for music files.
* Stream music directly from cloud storage.
* Play music without downloading the entire file first, where supported.
* Support seeking within tracks.
* Download selected songs for offline playback.
* Upload music from iPhone Files directly to cloud storage.
* Display cloud storage usage where the provider exposes it.
* Handle authentication expiry and reconnect when necessary.

Cloud integrations must use official APIs and comply with provider policies.

⸻

5. Cloud-First Music Management

This is one of the most important requirements.

I want cloud storage to act as my master music library.

The iPhone should primarily act as a playback device.

Expected behaviour:

* Music remains stored in cloud storage.
* Songs should stream when an internet connection is available.
* Songs should only be downloaded to iPhone when I explicitly request offline access.
* Downloaded songs should be available without internet.
* Deleting an offline download must NOT delete the original cloud file.
* Cloud originals should never be deleted automatically.
* Uploading a local file should preserve the original file.
* The application should clearly distinguish between cloud files and downloaded files.

Optional future feature:

A Smart Storage Manager that tracks local storage and helps remove old offline downloads while preserving cloud originals.

⸻

6. Audio Formats and Sound Quality

I want the application to prioritize high-quality audio playback.

Preferred formats:

* FLAC
* WAV
* ALAC
* MP3
* AAC

Requirements:

* Support lossless audio where technically possible.
* Preserve the original audio quality.
* Avoid unnecessary audio compression.
* Display audio information.
* Display codec, bitrate, sample rate and bit depth when available.
* Handle different audio formats correctly.
* Investigate additional codec libraries if native iOS support is insufficient.

Important: Do not claim that audio quality improves simply by increasing sample rate or bitrate.

⸻

7. Audio Player Features

The main music player should include:

* Play/Pause
* Next/Previous
* Seek bar
* Shuffle
* Repeat
* Queue management
* Background playback
* Lock-screen controls
* Control Centre integration
* Headphone controls
* Bluetooth audio support
* Gapless playback where supported
* Sleep timer
* Playback history
* Recently played songs
* Favourites

Additional features:

* Equalizer
* Bass Boost
* Custom equalizer profiles
* Volume normalization / ReplayGain where supported
* Crossfade
* Audio quality information

The application should continue playing music when the screen is locked or the user switches to another application.

⸻

8. Music Library Management

The library should automatically organize imported music.

Organize by:

* Songs
* Artists
* Albums
* Genres
* Playlists
* Favourites
* Recently Added
* Recently Played

Additional requirements:

* Search by song name.
* Search by artist.
* Search by album.
* Create custom playlists.
* Edit song information when appropriate.
* Display available album artwork.
* Maintain a consistent library across cloud and local sources.

Metadata should be extracted from available file tags. External artwork and metadata services should only be used where permitted.

⸻

9. Music Search and Download Requirements

I want to search for music from different Indian and international film industries.

Preferred languages:

* Kannada
* Hindi
* Tamil
* Telugu
* English

The long-term objective is to make it easy to find music and add it to my library.

However, the application must respect copyright and platform restrictions.

Important limitations:

* YouTube Data API can provide search results and metadata but does not authorize downloading arbitrary song audio.
* Do not use unofficial YouTube extractors or bypass platform restrictions.
* Commercial music must come from licensed sources or files I am legally authorized to use.
* Offline downloads must be supported only when the relevant source grants download rights.

The practical initial approach should prioritize music files that I own or am authorized to store and play.

⸻

10. Upload Music to Cloud

I want a dedicated upload feature.

Expected workflow:

1. Open SONORA.
2. Select Upload Music.
3. Open the iPhone Files picker.
4. Select one or multiple audio files.
5. Select the connected cloud provider.
6. Select the destination folder.
7. Upload the files.
8. Show upload progress.
9. Confirm successful upload.

The uploaded file should remain available in the cloud library.

⸻

11. Offline Music

I want the ability to select individual songs or albums for offline playback.

Requirements:

* Download selected songs.
* Download complete albums.
* Show download progress.
* Pause and resume downloads where possible.
* Display offline storage usage.
* Remove offline copies.
* Never delete cloud originals when removing local copies.

⸻

12. Apple CarPlay Support

I want SONORA to support both:

* Wired Apple CarPlay
* Wireless Apple CarPlay

CarPlay requirements:

* Display available music.
* Browse music library using supported CarPlay templates.
* Play and pause songs.
* Skip tracks.
* Browse playlists.
* Display track information.
* Support playback controls.

Important:

CarPlay integration requires the appropriate Apple entitlement and compliance with Apple’s CarPlay requirements.

Do not assume that simply installing a private iPhone application automatically enables CarPlay.

Design the application architecture to accommodate CarPlay, but verify entitlement eligibility and approval before promising availability.

Official documentation:
https://developer.apple.com/carplay/

⸻

13. Security and Privacy

* Secure OAuth authentication.
* Store tokens securely using iOS Keychain.
* Never hardcode cloud credentials.
* Use HTTPS.
* Respect provider permissions.
* Do not collect unnecessary personal information.
* Do not upload personal music without user consent.
* Make cloud account disconnection possible.
* Ensure users can remove locally stored data safely.

⸻

14. Monetization

My initial preference:

* No advertisements.
* No mandatory subscription.
* No unnecessary paid features.
* Use my own cloud storage accounts.

The app should not depend on a third-party music subscription for its basic functionality.

Cloud storage costs and provider restrictions are separate from the application’s own pricing.

