15. Development and Deployment

I have a Mac mini and an iPhone.

I want to develop the actual working application and install it on my iPhone.

Preferred development process:

Phase 1 – Foundation

* Set up Xcode project.
* Create SONORA interface.
* Implement local audio playback.
* Implement background playback.
* Test on iPhone.

Phase 2 – Library

* Implement music import.
* Read metadata.
* Create music library.
* Implement playlists and favourites.

Phase 3 – Cloud

* Google Drive integration.
* Dropbox integration.
* OneDrive integration.
* Investigate and implement MEGA integration.
* Implement cloud streaming.
* Implement uploads and offline downloads.

Phase 4 – Audio

* Equalizer.
* Bass Boost.
* Lossless format support.
* Audio information.
* Playback enhancements.

Phase 5 – CarPlay

* Investigate entitlement eligibility.
* Implement supported CarPlay interface if approved.
* Test on an actual CarPlay-compatible vehicle.

Phase 6 – Final Release

* Test thoroughly.
* Fix bugs.
* Optimize performance.
* Install on my iPhone.
* Prepare for potential App Store release.

For initial personal testing, investigate free Apple Developer Account deployment through Xcode.

For wider distribution and TestFlight/App Store publishing, explain the Apple Developer Program requirements and costs.

⸻

16. Important Development Instructions

Please follow these instructions throughout the project:

1. Build a real working application, not just a visual prototype.
2. Develop one phase at a time.
3. Explain where each piece of code belongs.
4. Provide complete code files when necessary.
5. Avoid giving incomplete code snippets that cannot be integrated.
6. Do not assume a feature works without testing it.
7. Clearly explain Apple, cloud provider and copyright limitations.
8. Prioritize a reliable music player before advanced features.
9. Keep the architecture modular so future features can be added.
10. Do not introduce unnecessary paid services.
11. Do not claim that the application has been deployed unless it has actually been installed and tested.

